adaptation-samsung-r7 (0.0.0+git20260720203123.c4c06d0.bookworm+git20260728092037.c349ebc.bookworm+r7spen1+r7dns1+r7setup1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Add the first-boot setup lock (OOBE). A wlr-layer-shell overlay
    (r7-setup-lock, GtkApplicationWindow + gtk4-layer-shell via LD_PRELOAD,
    cairo renderer) blocks the panel and all gestures and stays until every
    runtime patch of the port has settled — verified by readiness probes
    (ion perms, frame-pacing, audio HAL + sink, camera, S-Pen daemon, DNS,
    sensors), not a scripted step list. It shows no per-component narrative
    (the adaptation configures at build time, not first boot). Sequenced after
    GNOME Initial Setup via r7-setup-lock.path (so it never covers the Wi-Fi
    step its DNS probe depends on), gated by an idempotent completion stamp so
    it re-shows if the device reboots mid-setup. Depends on gtk4/adw/
    gtk4-layer-shell introspection. Proven end-to-end on device.

 -- Yunus Tan <yunus.tan@outlook.com.tr>  Sat, 01 Aug 2026 19:25:00 +0300

adaptation-samsung-r7 (0.0.0+git20260720203123.c4c06d0.bookworm+git20260728092037.c349ebc.bookworm+r7spen1+r7dns1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * configs.postinst: repoint /etc/resolv.conf at NetworkManager's resolv.conf.
    The rootfs ships it as a symlink to the systemd-resolved stub, but
    systemd-resolved is masked so that target never exists -> DNS was completely
    broken (WiFi up, 8.8.8.8 reachable, but nothing resolves). NetworkManager
    already writes /run/NetworkManager/resolv.conf (dns=default,
    rc-manager=symlink) but will not overwrite the pre-existing stub symlink, so
    it never took effect. Verified on-device: name resolution works once the
    symlink points at NM's file.

 -- Yunus Tan <yunus.tan@outlook.com.tr>  Sat, 01 Aug 2026 17:35:00 +0300

adaptation-samsung-r7 (0.0.0+git20260720203123.c4c06d0.bookworm+git20260728092037.c349ebc.bookworm+r7spen1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Ship the S-Pen deliverable that never made it into the packaged configs:
    the r7-spen-mode-daemon (tablet/touch toggle), its GSettings schema and
    Configurable-Tweaks override, the sec_e-pen hwdb resolution quirk (pen
    hover/tap/button), the uinput udev rule, the systemd user service, and the
    spen.yaml tweak. The phosh-mobile-settings toggle shipped without them, so
    it controlled a schema and daemon that did not exist.
  * configs.postinst: regenerate hwdb (systemd-hwdb update), compile the
    GSettings schema, and enable r7-spen-mode.service for all users.
  * configs: depend on python3-gi and python3-evdev (the daemon needs them).

